# The desktop contract is generated from the Rust DTOs and carries a protocol
# fingerprint hashed over the wire crates (see crates/ipc/build.rs), so any
# edit under crates/{ipc,core}/src rewrites these files — and a rebase across
# such an edit conflicts on them every time. The `lazybox-contract` merge
# driver regenerates them from the merged tree instead of leaving markers.
# Register it with `make setup` or `make install-merge-driver`; without it git
# falls back to a normal (conflicting) text merge, which `make rebase-main`
# then resolves the same way.
apps/desktop/src/generated/* merge=lazybox-contract
